{"Permissions cleanup on removal events (RoleRemovedEvent, ClientRemovedEvent, GroupRemovedEvent) now only runs when ADMIN_FINE_GRAINED_AUTHZ is enabled, which can leave stale permissions if the feature is disabled after being used or if resources are removed while it's off": 0.7398982048034668, "In ClientPermissionsV2, getEvaluationContext(...) is private and unused, and related imports/constants (e.g., AccessToken, EvaluationContext, ClientModelIdentity, TOKEN_EXCHANGE) appear unused as well": 0.6006326675415039, "Javadoc for requireView() incorrectly describes a boolean return value instead of the thrown exception behavior - should document that it throws ForbiddenException when canView() is false": 0.7891000509262085, "Missing tests to cover MAP_ROLES_CLIENT_SCOPE for clients - PermissionClientTest only covers MAP_ROLES and MAP_ROLES_COMPOSITE but not the new MAP_ROLES_CLIENT_SCOPE scope": 0.42767658829689026, "Missing REST-level tests to cover the new CLIENTS resource type and its identifier resolution (both client ID and clientId alias)": 0.51983243227005, "Several Javadoc comments in ClientPermissionEvaluator (e.g., requireView(), requireViewClientScopes()) describe the methods as returning a boolean even though they are void": 0.7511411905288696}